        "raw": "<p>Citizen Dawn is throwing down with the Freedom Five (Freedom Five Legacy, Freedom Five Wraith, Freedom Five Absolute Zero, Freedom Five Tachyon and Freedom Five Bunker) in Megalopolis.&nbsp; What could go wrong?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Not surprisingly, this is not a hard battle for the Freedom Five.&nbsp; I sorta accidentally took out all of Dawn's citizens at the end of round 1 (but the \"Hypersonic Assault\" card looked so *tempting*...) and Dawn flipped at the start of round 2.&nbsp; Opps - not what I was planning on doing.&nbsp; However, Wraith got \"Infrared Eyepiece\" out quickly and then manipulated Dawn's deck to speed the play of more citizens.&nbsp; Dawn flipped back at the start of round 5 and her citizens all went down the same round and Dawn did not last until the end of round 6.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Might try to see if I can play this again and delay or keep Dawn from flipping.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>[UPDATE: yeah, if you don't accidentally take all of the citizens off the field in round 1, it is very easy to take Dawn out without her ever flipping.&nbsp; Game took about the same number of turns (*maybe* 5 rounds instead of 6?) and the heroes' hit points are a touch lower, but still a good strong win.]</p>\r\n\r\n<p>For the most part, the environment wasn't too bad, which is about all you can hope for in Megalopolis.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>One big SPOILER below - read at your own risk.<br />\r\n.<br />\r\n.<br />\r\n.<br />\r\n.<br />\r\n.<br />\r\n.<br />\r\n.<br />\r\n.<br />\r\nDawn plays the well-named \"Devastating Aurora\" at the start of round 2.&nbsp; I had the heroes lose a lot of good setup due to that.&nbsp; But at least it took out the irritating \"Paparazzi On the Scene\" card the environment played on round 1.</p>",
